msgid "Activate or deactivate datasources"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When a datasource is configured at build time, and its URL is set at "
"runtime, it is active by default.\n"
"Quarkus starts the corresponding JDBC connection pool or reactive client "
"when the application starts."
msgstr ""

msgid "To deactivate a datasource at runtime, either:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Do not set `quarkus.datasource[.optional name].jdbc.url` or `quarkus."
"datasource[.optional name].reactive.url`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Set `quarkus.datasource[.optional name].active` to `false`."
msgstr ""

msgid "If a datasource is not active:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The datasource does not attempt to connect to the database during "
"application startup."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The datasource does not contribute a <<datasource-health-check,health "
"check>>."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Static CDI injection points involving the datasource, such as `@Inject "
"DataSource ds` or `@Inject Pool pool`, cause application startup to fail."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Dynamic retrieval of the datasource, such as through `CDI."
"getBeanContainer()`, `Arc.instance()`, or an injected "
"`Instance<DataSource>`, causes an exception to be thrown."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Other Quarkus extensions that consume the datasource can cause application "
"startup to fail."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In this case, you must also deactivate those other extensions.\n"
"To see an example of this scenario, refer to the xref:hibernate-orm."
"adoc#persistence-unit-active[Activate/deactivate persistence units] section "
"of the Hibernate ORM guide.\n"
"For Hibernate ORM, Quarkus deactivates the persistence unit when the "
"datasource is inactive."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This feature is especially useful when the application must select one "
"datasource from a predefined set at runtime."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Setting `quarkus.datasource.\"pg\".active=true` xref:config-reference."
"adoc#configuration-sources[at runtime] makes only the PostgreSQL datasource "
"available.\n"
"Setting `quarkus.datasource.\"oracle\".active=true` at runtime makes only "
"the Oracle datasource available."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"xref:config-reference.adoc#custom-profiles[Custom configuration profiles] "
"simplify this setup.\n"
"By appending the following profile-specific configuration to the one above, "
"you can select a persistence unit or datasource at runtime by xref:config-"
"reference.adoc#multiple-profiles[setting `quarkus.profile`].\n"
"For example, use `quarkus.profile=prod,pg` or `quarkus.profile=prod,oracle`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"With this setup, ensure that only the _active_ datasource is accessed.\n"
"To achieve this, inject an `InjectableInstance<DataSource>` or "
"`InjectableInstance<Pool>` with an `@Any` qualifier and call xref:cdi-"
"integration.adoc#inactive-synthetic-beans[`getActive()`]."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Alternatively, define a xref:cdi.adoc#ok-you-said-that-there-are-several-"
"kinds-of-beans[CDI bean producer] for the default datasource.\n"
"The bean producer redirects to the active named datasource.\n"
"The application can then inject the default datasource directly, as shown "
"below:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Do not inject a `DataSource` or `AgroalDataSource` directly.\n"
"Injecting inactive beans causes a startup failure.\n"
"Instead, inject `InjectableInstance<DataSource>` or "
"`InjectableInstance<AgroalDataSource>`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Declare a CDI producer method to define the default datasource.\n"
"It selects either PostgreSQL or Oracle, depending on which one is active."
msgstr ""

msgid "Check if a bean is active before retrieving it."
msgstr ""

msgid "Injects the only active datasource."
msgstr ""

msgid "Use multiple datasources in a single transaction"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"By default, XA support on datasources is disabled.\n"
"Therefore, a transaction can include no more than one datasource.\n"
"Attempting to access multiple non-XA datasources in the same transaction "
"results in an exception similar to the following:"
msgstr ""

msgid "To allow using multiple JDBC datasources in the same transaction:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Make sure your JDBC driver supports XA.\n"
"All <<extensions-and-database-drivers-reference,supported JDBC drivers do>>, "
"but <<other-databases,other JDBC drivers>> might not."
msgstr ""

msgid "Make sure your database server is configured to enable XA."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Enable XA support explicitly for each relevant datasource by setting "
"<<quarkus-agroal_quarkus-datasource-jdbc-transactions,`quarkus.datasource[."
"optional name].jdbc.transactions`>> to `xa`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Using XA, a rollback in one datasource will trigger a rollback in every "
"other datasource enrolled in the transaction."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"XA transactions on reactive datasources are not supported at the moment."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If your transaction involves non-datasource resources, be aware that they "
"might not support XA transactions or might require additional configuration."
msgstr ""

msgid "If XA cannot be enabled for one of your datasources:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Be aware that enabling XA for all datasources _except one_ (and only one) is "
"still supported through link:https://www.narayana.io/docs/project/index."
"html#_last_resource_commit_optimization_lrco[Last Resource Commit "
"Optimization (LRCO)]."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If you do not need a rollback for one datasource to trigger a rollback for "
"other datasources, consider splitting your code into multiple transactions.\n"
"To do so, use xref:transaction.adoc#programmatic-"
"approach[`QuarkusTransaction.requiringNew()`]/xref:transaction."
"adoc#declarative-approach[`@Transactional(REQUIRES_NEW)`] (preferably) or "
"xref:transaction.adoc#legacy-api-approach[`UserTransaction`] (for more "
"complex use cases)."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If no other solution works and compatibility with Quarkus 3.8 or earlier is "
"required, set `quarkus.transaction-manager.unsafe-multiple-last-resources` "
"to `allow` to enable unsafe transaction handling across multiple non-XA "
"datasources."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"With this property set to `allow`, a transaction rollback might only apply "
"to the last non-XA datasource, while other non-XA datasources may have "
"already committed their changes.\n"
"This can leave the system in an inconsistent state."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Alternatively, allow the same unsafe behavior but with warnings when it "
"occurs:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Setting the property to `warn-each` logs a warning for *each* offending "
"transaction."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Setting the property to `warn-first` logs a warning for the *first* "
"offending transaction."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"We do not recommend using this configuration property and plan to remove it "
"in the future.\n"
"You should update your application accordingly.\n"
"If you believe your use case justifies keeping this option, open an issue in "
"the link:https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/issues/new?assignees=&labels="
"kind%2Fenhancement&projects=&template=feature_request.yml[Quarkus tracker] "
"explaining why."
msgstr ""

msgid "Datasource integrations"
msgstr ""

msgid "Datasource health check"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If you use the link:https://quarkus.io/extensions/io.quarkus/quarkus-"
"smallrye-health[`quarkus-smallrye-health`] extension, the `quarkus-agroal` "
"and reactive client extensions automatically add a readiness health check to "
"validate the datasource."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When you access your application’s health readiness endpoint, `/q/health/"
"ready` by default, you receive information about the datasource validation "
"status.\n"
"If you have multiple datasources, all datasources are checked, and if a "
"single datasource validation failure occurs, the status changes to `DOWN`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can disable this behavior by setting `quarkus.datasource.health.enabled="
"false`."
msgstr ""

msgid "To exclude only a particular datasource from the health check:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Datasource metrics"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When you add the xref:telemetry-micrometer.adoc[`quarkus-micrometer`] "
"extension, `quarkus-agroal` can publish datasource metrics to the metrics "
"registry.\n"
"To enable these metrics, set `quarkus.datasource.metrics.enabled=true`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For the published metrics to report values, Agroal must enable its internal "
"metrics collection.\n"
"By default, Agroal enables internal metrics collection for all datasources "
"when a metrics extension is present and `quarkus.datasource.metrics.enabled` "
"is set to `true`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To disable metrics for a specific datasource, set `quarkus.datasource.jdbc."
"metrics.enabled=false`.\n"
"For a named datasource, set `quarkus.datasource.<datasource name>.jdbc."
"metrics.enabled=false`.\n"
"This setting stops internal metrics collection and stops exposing datasource "
"metrics at the `/q/metrics` endpoint."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To enable internal metrics collection explicitly for the default data "
"source, set `quarkus.datasource.jdbc.metrics.enabled=true`.\n"
"To enable internal metrics collection explicitly for a named data source, "
"set `quarkus.datasource.<datasource name>.jdbc.metrics.enabled=true`.\n"
"This enables internal metrics collection even when you do not add a metrics "
"extension.\n"
"You can access the collected metrics programmatically by calling `dataSource."
"getMetrics()` on an injected `AgroalDataSource` instance."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When metrics collection is disabled for a data source, all metric values are "
"zero."
msgstr ""

msgid "Datasource tracing"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To use tracing with a datasource, you need to add the xref:opentelemetry-"
"tracing.adoc[`quarkus-opentelemetry`] extension to your project."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You do not need to declare a different driver to enable tracing.\n"
"If you use a JDBC driver, you need to follow xref:opentelemetry-tracing."
"adoc#jdbc[the instructions in the OpenTelemetry extension]."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Even with all the tracing infrastructure in place, the datasource tracing is "
"not enabled by default, and you need to enable it by setting this property:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"By default, only SQL statement executions are traced.\n"
"Connection acquisition from the datasource (`getConnection()` calls) is not "
"traced.\n"
"To also trace connection acquisition, enable it explicitly:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Narayana transaction manager integration"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Integration is automatic if the Narayana JTA extension is also available."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can override this by setting the `transactions` configuration property:"
msgstr ""

msgid "`quarkus.datasource.jdbc.transactions` for default unnamed datasource"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`quarkus.datasource._<datasource-name>_.jdbc.transactions` for named "
"datasource"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When a datasource is configured for XA transactions by setting `quarkus."
"datasource[.optional name].jdbc.transactions=xa` and the transaction "
"recovery system is enabled by using `quarkus.transaction-manager.enable-"
"recovery=true`, the datasource is automatically registered for recovery.\n"
"This is the preferred and safe default.\n"
"You can override this behavior for individual datasources by setting "
"`quarkus.datasource.jdbc.enable-recovery=false` or `quarkus.datasource."
"\"datasource-name\".jdbc.enable-recovery=false`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Change this setting only in advanced use cases and only if you are certain "
"recovery is not required.\n"
"Incorrect configuration can lead to data loss, data unavailability, or both, "
"due to resources remaining locked indefinitely."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For more information, see the <<configuration-reference,Configuration "
"reference>> section below.\n"
"To facilitate the storage of transaction logs in a database by using JDBC, "
"see the xref:transaction.adoc#jdbcstore[Configuring transaction logs to be "
"stored in a datasource] section of the xref:transaction.adoc[Using "
"transactions in Quarkus] guide."
msgstr ""

msgid "Testing with in-memory databases"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The recommended approach for testing against databases is to use the same "
"database as production to get test results that match production behavior as "
"closely as possible.\n"
"xref:databases-dev-services.adoc[Dev Services] simplifies this approach by "
"requiring no configuration and starting quickly."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For scenarios where neither Dev Services nor a custom database setup is "
"possible, you can use a JVM based database such as H2 in embedded mode."
msgstr ""

msgid "Support and limitations"
msgstr ""

msgid "Embedded databases such as H2 work in JVM mode."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In native mode, do not embed H2 in the native image.\n"
"Use a remote connection to a separate database, or use Dev Services to run "
"the database outside the native image."
msgstr ""

msgid "Run an integration test"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Add a dependency on the artifacts providing the additional tools that are "
"under the following Maven coordinates:"
msgstr ""

msgid "`io.quarkus:quarkus-test-h2` for H2"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can test your application even when it is compiled into a native "
"executable, while the database will run as a JVM process."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Add the following annotation to any class in your integration tests to run "
"the tests on both the JVM and native executables:"
msgstr ""

msgid "`@QuarkusTestResource(H2DatabaseTestResource.class)`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This ensures that the test suite starts and terminates the managed database "
"in a separate process as required for test execution."
msgstr ""

