msgid ""
"Each supported database has its own JDBC URL configuration options.\n"
"The following sections describe each JDBC URL and provide a link to the "
"official documentation."
msgstr ""

msgid "DB2"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`jdbc:db2://<serverName>[:<portNumber>]/<databaseName>[:<key1>="
"<value>;[<key2>=<value2>;]]`"
msgstr ""

msgid "Example"
msgstr ""

msgid "`jdbc:db2://localhost:50000/MYDB:user=dbadm;password=dbadm;`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For more information on URL syntax and additional supported options, see the "
"link:https://www.ibm.com/docs/en/db2/12.1.x?topic=cdsudidsdjs-url-format-"
"data-server-driver-jdbc-sqlj-type-4-connectivity[official documentation]."
msgstr ""

msgid "H2"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`jdbc:h2:{ {.|mem:}[name] | [file:]fileName | {tcp|ssl}:[//]server[:"
"port][,server2[:port]]/name }[;key=value...]`"
msgstr ""

msgid "`jdbc:h2:tcp://localhost/~/test`, `jdbc:h2:mem:myDB`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"H2 is a database that can run in embedded or server mode.\n"
"It can use a file storage or run entirely in memory.\n"
"All of these options are available as listed above."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For more information, see the link:https://h2database.com/html/features."
"html#database_url[official documentation]."
msgstr ""

msgid "MariaDB"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`jdbc:mariadb:[replication:|failover:|sequential:|aurora:]//"
"<hostDescription>[,<hostDescription>...]/[database][?<key1>=<value1>[&<key2>="
"<value2>]]`\n"
"hostDescription:: `<host>[:<portnumber>] or address=(host=<host>)[(port="
"<portnumber>)][(type=(master|slave))]`"
msgstr ""

msgid "`jdbc:mariadb://localhost:3306/test`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For more information, see the link:https://mariadb.com/docs/connectors/"
"mariadb-connector-j/[official documentation]."
msgstr ""

msgid "Microsoft SQL server"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`jdbc:sqlserver://[serverName[\\instanceName][:portNumber]][;property="
"value[;property=value]]`"
msgstr ""

msgid "`jdbc:sqlserver://localhost:1433;databaseName=AdventureWorks`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For more information, see the link:https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/sql/"
"connect/jdbc/connecting-to-sql-server-with-the-jdbc-driver?view=sql-server-"
"ver16[official documentation]."
msgstr ""

msgid "MySQL"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`jdbc:mysql:[replication:|failover:|sequential:|aurora:]//"
"<hostDescription>[,<hostDescription>...]/[database][?<key1>=<value1>[&<key2>="
"<value2>]]`\n"
"hostDescription:: `<host>[:<portnumber>] or address=(host=<host>)[(port="
"<portnumber>)][(type=(master|slave))]`"
msgstr ""

msgid "`jdbc:mysql://localhost:3306/test`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For more information, see the link:https://dev.mysql.com/doc/connector-j/en/"
"[official documentation]."
msgstr ""

msgid "MySQL limitations"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When you compile an application into a native image, the following "
"limitations apply to MySQL Connector/J integrations:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus disables Java Management Extensions (JMX) support because it does "
"not work in native mode."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus disables Oracle Cloud Infrastructure (OCI) integration because it "
"does not work in native mode."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus disables the MySQL Connector/J OpenTelemetry integration and relies "
"on the Agroal integration instead."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If you need the MySQL Connector/J OpenTelemetry integration, enable it "
"explicitly by setting `quarkus.datasource.jdbc.additional-jdbc-properties."
"openTelemetry=PREFERRED`.\n"
"For more information, see link:https://dev.mysql.com/doc/connector-j/en/"
"connector-j-connp-props-debugging-profiling.html#cj-conn-"
"prop_openTelemetry[MySQL Connector/J documentation]."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When you enable this option and also add the `quarkus-opentelemetry` "
"extension, the application can fail to start and throw a `java.lang."
"IllegalStateException: GlobalOpenTelemetry.set has already been called.` "
"error."
msgstr ""

msgid "Oracle"
msgstr ""

